\par
\cf2\b System Volume Button\cf0\b0\par
The Volume button lets you adjust your computer\rquote s system volume directly from inside Skye Music. Instead of changing only the player\rquote s mute state, this button now controls the actual Windows volume level, so everything you hear on your device stays consistent. The button shows the current system volume, and the wheel on your mouse changes the volume when you hover over it. Any changes you make here apply instantly to your whole system, not just the app.\par
\par
The button also includes a quick mute toggle. If you need to silence everything immediately, you can tap the button and Windows will mute all audio at once. Tapping it again restores your previous volume level. Skye Music stays in sync with your computer, so if you change the volume using your keyboard or the taskbar, the button updates automatically to match whatever the system is doing.\par
\par
Skye Music also supports Volume Boost for quiet videos or recordings. When you scroll past 100%, the player can raise audio up to 150% using its internal amplifier. To make this feel natural, the volume control briefly \ldblquote pauses\rdblquote  at 100% before entering boost mode, so you don\rquote t jump into amplified audio by accident. Boost affects only Skye Music\rquote s playback and does not change your system\rquote s maximum volume.\par
\par
This makes volume control feel more natural and predictable, especially when switching between apps or using hardware keys. The button always reflects the real system state, and Boost Mode gives you extra headroom when you need it.\par
\par
\cf2\b Managing Playlists\cf0\b0\par
To create, rename, reorder, or delete playlists, open Options and select the Playlists tab. Each playlist is stored as an individual file, allowing you to easily organize distinct music collections. Select your active Playlist by clicking the drop-down in the upper-right of the Player window, just above the playlist.\par
\par
\cf2\b Audio Settings & Volume Boost\cf0\b0\par
Skye Music gives you control over how audio is delivered to your speakers through the "Enable Volume Boost" option in Settings.\par
\par
\i Enable Volume Boost (Checked)\i0\par
When checked, Skye Music uses the DirectSound audio engine. This mode allows you to push player volume beyond 100%, making it ideal for quiet recordings or low-gain audio files that need extra volume. Note that on some PCs, high volume boost or heavy system loads can occasionally cause subtle audio pops or crackling.\par
\par
\i High Stability Mode (Unchecked)\i0\par
When unchecked, Skye Music uses the modern WASAPI audio engine. This mode provides clean, crystal-clear, distortion-free sound and maximum playback stability across all system conditions. To prevent digital audio clipping, volume is capped at a maximum of 100% in this mode.\par
\par
\i Will toggling Volume Boost interrupt my playing song?\i0\par
No. Skye Music automatically restarts the audio engine in the background and resumes your music at the exact second you left off.\par
\par
\i Why did my volume automatically drop to 100% when I unchecked Volume Boost?\i0\par
WASAPI mode enforces a 100% volume limit to ensure clean sound without clipping. If your volume was set above 100%, Skye Music automatically adjusts it back down to 100%.\par
\par
