\par
\cf2\b Playlist Track Exclusion\cf0\b0\par
You can exclude individual tracks from active playback without removing them from your playlist.\par
\par
\i How to Toggle\i0\par
Right-click a track and select Exclude or Include.\par
\par
\i Playback Behavior\i0\par
Excluded tracks are automatically skipped during normal auto-play and when using the Next/Previous buttons.\par
\par
\i Direct Selection\i0\par
Double-clicking an excluded track will still play it directly.\par
\par
\i Playlist Exporting\i0\par
Excluded tracks are automatically filtered out when exporting your playlist.\par
\par
\cf2\b MiniPlayer\cf0\b0\par
The MiniPlayer is a compact, always\f2\_on\_top version of Skye\f1\lang1033  \f2\lang9 Music designed for quick access, clean visuals, and minimal screen footprint. It gives you the essential\f1\lang1033 s: \f2\lang9 playback controls, \f1\lang1033 album art, \f2\lang9 track information, and a visualizer\f1\lang1033 , \f2\lang9 while staying out of your way.\f1\lang1033  \f2\lang9 The MiniPlayer is designed to keep Skye\f1\lang1033  \f2\lang9 Music visible while you work, browse, or game, offering a lightweight way to enjoy visualizers without opening the full window. It can be tucked neatly into a corner of your screen, making it perfect as a small \ldblquote desk companion\rdblquote  version of the app that stays out of the way while still giving you quick access to playback and visuals. The MiniPlayer is intentionally simple\f1\lang1033  \f2\lang9 and unobtrusive.\par
\par
You can open the MiniPlayer from the main player\rquote s menu, from the tray icon by\b  \f1\lang1033 <D\f2\lang9 ouble\_\f1\lang1033 C\f2\lang9 lick\f1\lang1033 >\b0\f2\lang9 ing it, or by using the keyboard shortcut \b\f1\lang1033 <\f2\lang9 P\f1\lang1033 >\b0\f2\lang9 . \b\f1\lang1033 <ESC> \b0 or \b <P> \b0 will close the MiniPlayer and reopen the Player. \f2\lang9 Closing the MiniPlayer never stops playback; it simply hides the compact view and hands control back to the main window, letting your music continue uninterrupted.\par
\par
Each visualizer offers an \f1\lang1033 "\f2\lang9 Allow MiniMode\f1\lang1033 "\f2\lang9  setting; when enabled, the MiniPlayer uses a version of the visualizer specifically optimized for small spaces, and when disabled, it displays the full visualizer exactly as it appears in the main window\f1\lang1033 , just in a smaller space.\par
\par
\cf2\b\lang9 Speech Recognition\par
\cf0\b0\lang1033 Your player includes an integrated speech recognition engine, allowing you to control media playback and adjust system settings entirely hands-free.\par
\par
\i Setting Up Push-to-Talk (PTT)\par
\i0 To prevent accidental voice triggers, voice recognition uses a customizable Push-to-Talk (PTT) shortcut.\par
- Open Settings and navigate to the App tab.\par
- Check Enable Voice Commands and Use Push-To-Talk.\par
- Click inside the Push-to-Talk Hotkey box.\par
- Press your desired key combination (e.g., Ctrl + Shift + V or Alt + Space).\par
- Click OK.\par
\par
\i How To Use\i0\par
- Press your configured hotkey and speak a command.\par
- The system audio will automatically "duck" to 20% so you can speak your command.\par
- The system audio is automatically returned to previous level.\par
- If no command is spoken or recognized, the player will automatically raise the system volume back up to the previous level after a short time.\par
\par
\i Voice Commands Reference\i0\par
- All commands must begin with "Hey Skye" in order to be recognized.\par
- "Play Music" plays the currently selected song.\par
- "Pause Music" pauses the current song.\par
- "Stop Music" stops playing the current song.\par
- "Previous Song" plays the last song in sequence or the previously played song.\par
- "Next Song" plays the next song according to the Play Mode.\par
- "Search" enters whatever words follow into the Playlist search box.\par
- "PlayMode Once" sets the PlayMode to play once and stop.\par
- "PlayMode Repeat" sets the PlayMode to repeat the current song indefinitely.\par
- "PlayMode Linear" sets the PlayMode to play the next song in the playlist.\par
- "PlayMode Shuffle" sets the PlayMode to play a random song.\par
- "Volume Up" increases the system volume by 10%.\par
- "Volume Down" decreases the system volume by 10%.\par
- Speaking the playlist title, or part of a title, will play that song. For example, saying "Hey Skye Taylor Swift" will play the first song found by Taylor Swift. Saying "Hey Skye [song name]" will play that song. You can also say the entire playlist title to play that song or stream. The grammar list is dependent on you playlist setup, and respects your separators and other settings for playlist organization. If the word or phrase is not in the playlist, the Speech Recognition Engine can't listen for it. In other words, you can't play by tag info or file name, only by what exists in the playlist.\par
\par
\i Smart Audio Ducking\i0\par
When Push-to-Talk is active, the app automatically ducks (lowers) your background system volume so the microphone can clearly detect your voice without interference from playing media.\par
- The system volume is automatically restored after a time or a command to its previous level. \par
- Smart Volume Control: If you give a command like "Volume Up" while using PTT, the baseline is adjusted in the background. Once PTT ends, your audio will restore to the newly adjusted level.\par
- Safe Shutdown Protection: If the application is closed while PTT is active, your system volume is automatically restored so your sound never remains stuck at a low level.\par
\par
\cf2\b\lang9 Stream & Podcast Directory\par
\cf0\b0\f2 The Directory is Skye\f1\lang1033  \f2\lang9 Music\rquote s unified browser for discovering, playing, and managing online radio stations and podcast feeds. It provides fast search, clean filtering, and full transparency about each station or podcast\rquote s available streams, episodes, and metadata.\par
\par
\i What You Can Do\i0\par
- Browse thousands of radio stations from supported sources\par
- Search stations by name, tags, country, format, or bitrate\par
- View bitrate, format, and status at a glance\par
- Select from multiple stream URLs when a station offers more than one\par
- Play a station immediately or add it to your playlist\par
- Save stations as favorites\par
- Browse podcasts from supported directories\par
- View podcast artwork, title, author, and categories\par
- Load episodes from any valid RSS feed\par
- Play podcast episodes directly or download them for offline listening\par
- Manually import any podcast feed URL\par
\par
\i Radio Station Columns\i0\par
- Name \endash  The station\rquote s display name\par
- Tags \endash  Keywords describing the station\rquote s genre or style\par
- Format \endash  The audio format (MP3, AAC, etc.)\par
- Bitrate \endash  The stream\rquote s quality level\par
- Country \endash  The station\rquote s origin\par
- Status \endash  Whether the station is currently online\par
- URL \endash  The stream URL used for playback\par
- (\f3\u9662?\f1 ) \f2\endash  Indicates the station has multiple stream options\par
\par
\i Selecting a Stream\i0\par
Some stations provide more than one stream (for example, different bitrates or formats).\par
To choose a specific stream:\par
- Click the \f3\u9662?\f1  More column for that station\par
- A menu appears listing all available streams\par
- Each entry shows the bitrate, format, and a shortened version of the URL\par
- Click the stream you want to use\par
SkyeMusic updates the URL column automatically and uses your selection for playback.\par
\par
\i Podcast Browsing\i0\par
When browsing podcasts, Skye Music displays:\par
- Artwork\par
- Title\par
- Author\par
- Category\par
- Feed URL\par
Selecting a podcast loads its episode list, including:\par
- Episode title\par
- Publish date\par
- Description (when available)\par
- Media URL\par
Episodes can be streamed immediately or downloaded for offline playback.\par
\par
\i Manual Podcast Feed Import\i0\par
Skye Music supports manual import of any valid RSS feed.\par
To add a feed:\par
- Select Add Podcast Feed from the source list\par
- Enter the feed\rquote s URL\par
- Skye Music loads the podcast\rquote s metadata and episodes automatically\par
This works with most podcast hosts, private feeds, and many YouTube channel RSS feeds.\par
\par
\i Right\f2\_Click Menus\i0\par
Right\_clicking a station or episode opens the context menu, allowing you to:\par
- Play immediately\par
- Add to playlist\par
- Add to favorites\par
- Copy the stream or episode URL\par
- Download podcast episodes (when supported)\par
\par
\i How Playlist Stream URLs Are Handled\i0\par
Skye\f1\lang1033  \f2\lang9 Music resolves playlist files (.pls, .m3u, .m3u8) automatically and shows you the direct streams they contain.\par
This ensures:\par
- Faster playback\par
- More reliable history entries\par
- No hidden or unstable URLs\par
If a station provides multiple streams, Skye\f1\lang1033  \f2\lang9 Music will choose a suitable option automatically, but you can always override it using the dropdown menu.\par
\par
\i Notes\i0\par
- The Directory updates automatically when switching sources\par
- Some stations may appear offline if their streams are temporarily unavailable\par
- Stream URLs can change over time; selecting a fresh one usually resolves playback issues\par
- Podcast feeds vary widely; artwork or metadata may not always be available\par
\par
\cf2\b\f1 Stream Metadata Support\cf0\b0\f4\par
Skye\f5\lang1033  \f4\lang9 Music can display \ldblquote Now Playing\rdblquote  information for many online radio stations. When a station provides track metadata, Skye\f5\lang1033  \f4\lang9 Music automatically reads and updates it while you listen.\par
\par
Some stations, such as SomaFM, publish their track information separately from the audio stream. Skye\f5\lang1033  \f4\lang9 Music includes built\_in support for these stations and will show artist and title information whenever it\rquote s available.\par
\par
If a station does not provide metadata, or provides only partial information, Skye\f5\lang1033  \f4\lang9 Music will simply display the station \f5\lang1033 title and URL from the playlist\f4\lang9  instead. This behavior is normal and depends entirely on what the station broadcasts.\f2\par
\par
\cf2\b\f1 Database Maintenance\cf0\b0\f4\par
\f1\lang1033 In the App section of Options, there is a button to perform basic maintenance on the Play History database file. This database tracks the play history of each song. Even though this database could easily contain thousands of records, it is only necessary to run the maintenance occasionally. The task takes only a second to run.\f2\lang9  \par
\par
\cf2\b\f1 Companion Server\cf0\b0\f4\par
\f2 Skye\f1\lang1033  \f2\lang9 Music includes a built\_in Companion Server that lets you control playback from other \f1\lang1033 Android or Windows \f2\lang9 device\f1\lang1033 s\f2\lang9  using the Skye\f1\lang1033  \f2\lang9 Music Companion App. When enabled, your PC will accept connections from \f1\lang1033 other devices \f2\lang9 on your local network.\f1\lang1033\par
\par
\f2\lang9 Connected devices appear in the Companion Clients window\f1\lang1033  accessed through the View menu. T\f2\lang9 here you can view basic information about each device, copy its name or IP address, or disconnect it if needed.\par
\par
The Companion Server is optional and can be turned on or off at any time in \f1\lang1033 Options.\par
\f2\lang9\par
\cf2\b\f1 Streaming Server\par
\cf0\b0\f2 Skye Music includes a built-in local network audio server that allows you to stream your live music playback directly to other computers, mobile devices, web browsers, media players (such as VLC)\f1\lang1033 , or the Companion App\f2\lang9  connected to the same local area network (LAN).\par
\par
\i Overview & How It Works\i0\par
When enabled, Skye Music captures its raw audio output and broadcasts it over a high-efficiency TCP/HTTP socket stream. Any device on your home or studio network can connect to your PC's IP address and listen to your playback in real time with minimal latency.\par
\par
\i Quick Start: Connecting a Client\i0\par
\f1\lang1033 - \f2\lang9 Find your Host IP Address\f1\lang1033  & e\f2\lang9 nsure the host computer running Skye Music is connected to your local Wi-Fi or Ethernet network.\par
\f1\lang1033 - \f2\lang9 Open a web browser or network media player (e.g., VLC, Chrome, Safari, or a mobile stream app) on your remote device.\par
\f1\lang1033 - \f2\lang9 Navigate to your streaming address using your host PC's local IP address and configured port:\f1\lang1033  {{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK http://<YOUR-PC-IP-ADDRESS>:<PORT>/live }}{\fldrslt{http://<YOUR-PC-IP-ADDRESS>:<PORT>/live\ul0\cf0}}}}\f1\fs24 . Examples: {{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK http://10.0.0.100:5051/live }}{\fldrslt{http://10.0.0.100:5051/live\ul0\cf0}}}}\f1\fs24 , or {{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK http://192.168.1.150:8080/live }}{\fldrslt{http://192.168.1.150:8080/live\ul0\cf0}}}}\f1\fs24 .\f2\lang9\par
\par
\i Managing Active Listeners\par
\i0\f1\lang1033 A tab has been added to the Clients window to montior listener connections. Information on the connection is provided, like connected IP Address, and data sent.\par
\f2\lang9\par
If an unwanted or stale connection remains active on your network:\par
\f1\lang1033 - \f2\lang9 Right-click any client entry in the Listener\f1\lang1033 s\f2\lang9  list.\par
\f1\lang1033 - \f2\lang9 Select Disconnect Client from the context menu.\par
\f1\lang1033 - \f2\lang9 Skye Music will instantly terminate the TCP socket for that client and free up server resources.\par
\par
\i Understanding Server Status Messages\i0\par
The \f1\lang1033 Playlist Status B\f2\lang9 ar \f1\lang1033 will \f2\lang9 display real-time feedback on the server engine state\f1\lang1033 .\par
- Stream Idle. This means the server is running.\par
- Stream Ready. This means a song is playing and the server is listening for new connections.\par
- Stream Live (x listeners). This tells you one or more streams are active.\par
\par
Options\par
The audio streaming server can be enabled or disabled in the App tab of the Options window. You can also configure the Port # and the target bitrate for the streams.\par
\par
Troubleshooting & Network Tips\par
- Windows Firewall Prompt. The first time you launch the streaming server, Windows Defender Firewall may ask for permission. Be sure to check Private networks to allow local devices to reach Skye Music.\par
- No Audio on Client. Ensure Skye Music is actively playing a track. If the player is paused, the stream will play silence until playback resumes.\par
- Router / Subnet Limits. Ensure your remote device (phone, tablet, laptop, secondary PC) is connected to the exact same Wi-Fi network/subnet as the host computer.\par
\par
\cf2\b\lang9 Streaming via the Companion App\par
\cf0\b0\lang1033 The Companion App allows you to stream your music server's audio directly to your device.\par
\par
\i How To Stream\par
\i0 - Configure your audio streaming port number in the app's Settings.\par
- Tap the streaming button on the far right of the volume slider on the home page to start or stop the live stream.\f2\lang9\par
